# This host's trust root for signatures (ADR-008; ADR-025 amendment 3). The HOST authors it -- by hand,
# or through `signer --setup`, which only the owner runs, in their own terminal; no other act of the kit
# writes it. One line per signer, in OpenSSH allowed_signers form:
#   <principal> [namespaces="<n>,..."] <key-type> <public-key>
# `agent-kit-capability` is the namespace a capability's publisher signs in; `git` is the one an owner's
# commits are signed in -- a line restricted to one is never a signer in the other. As seeded it names
# nobody, so no signature can be established on this host -- and every taken capability says so, as
# `no-trust-root`, rather than being called verified.
